[S03] He might maybe go on a little bit of a boozer of a weekend.

213
00:12:41.669 --> 00:12:42.899
[S03] Maybe he's panicking.

214
00:12:42.929 --> 00:12:45.860
[S03] He's just stressing about it to anyone who will listen.

215
00:12:45.889 --> 00:12:52.429
[S03] He's in a spiral of negativity and he's wasting all of this time worrying, constricting

216
00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:57.269
[S03] his focus, that he, he's so drained that he actually doesn't have the internal drive,

217
00:12:57.299 --> 00:13:03.220
[S03] resources, clarity or perspective to take action that's going to help him.

218
00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:05.990
[S03] So he kind of just ends up in this downward spiral.

219
00:13:06.019 --> 00:13:11.279
[S03] And then he does end up in a difficult situation financially and he ends up manifesting exactly

220
00:13:11.309 --> 00:13:13.879
[S03] the worst case scenario that he was thinking about.

221
00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.639
[S04] Maybe this means I'm meant for more.

222
00:13:51.669 --> 00:13:53.879
[S04] Maybe this means I should put myself out there.

223
00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:57.519
[S04] And because he's thinking on that level and he's feeling on that level,

224
00:13:57.549 --> 00:14:00.480
[S04] his body starts taking action on that level.

225
00:14:00.879 --> 00:14:05.039
[S04] And so he remembers all of a sudden because his perspective is open

226
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:07.840
[S04] and he's vibrationally in alignment through his thoughts and emotions.

227
00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:11.679
[S04] He remembers all of a sudden, I had a call with a man six months ago

228
00:14:11.799 --> 00:14:14.120
[S04] and he told me about this really interesting opportunity.

229
00:14:14.149 --> 00:14:15.519
[S04] Let me give him a call.

230
00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:17.360
[S04] So Eric remembers this thing.

231
00:14:17.389 --> 00:14:18.440
[S04] He calls the guy.

232
00:14:19.279 --> 00:14:21.789
[S04] John might have had a conversation with someone six months ago as well,

233
00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:23.759
[S04] but John can't see that or remember that

234
00:14:23.789 --> 00:14:25.879
[S04] because his energy is not in alignment with it, right?

235
00:14:25.899 --> 00:14:27.240
[S04] Because he's in that survival state.

236
00:14:27.399 --> 00:14:29.919
[S04] But Eric can remember it because he's open to his perception.

237
00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:31.399
[S04] And so he calls the guy.

238
00:14:31.429 --> 00:14:33.679
[S04] The guy puts him in touch with someone else, sets up a job.

239
00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:36.159
[S04] Next thing you know, Eric is feeling amazing

240
00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:39.879
[S04] because he's suddenly got an amazing opportunity lined up for himself, right?

241
00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:43.960
[S04] And so you see how these two situations, the situation is the same,

242
00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:48.799
[S04] but the response is different because the person interpreting the situation

243
00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:50.879
[S04] is in a different state.

244
00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.309
[S04] That is what it always comes down to.

245
00:14:53.639 --> 00:14:55.720
[S04] It's not about what happens to you.

246
00:14:55.879 --> 00:14:57.559
[S04] It's about how you respond.

247
00:14:57.759 --> 00:15:01.879
[S04] And most people are reacting impulsively on autopilot

248
00:15:01.909 --> 00:15:04.279
[S04] because they don't have the capacity to respond

249
00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:07.230
[S04] because they are in a survival mode and everything feels like a threat.

250
00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:09.720
[S04] So they just feel like they're constantly reacting.

251
00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:11.679
[S04] They have no control over themselves.

252
00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:14.559
[S04] So that is what regulation will do for you.

253
00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:17.639
[S04] It gives you the power to open your awareness

254
00:15:17.669 --> 00:15:22.559
[S04] and respond in alignment with the outcome that you prefer.

255
00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:25.600
[S04] That is manifestation.

256
00:15:25.629 --> 00:15:27.159
[S04] That is reality creation.

257
00:15:27.519 --> 00:15:29.639
[S04] So if you're in survival mode, essentially

258
00:15:29.669 --> 00:15:32.320
[S04] you are in a state of chronic activation

259
00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.559
[S04] or dysregulation in your nervous system.

260
00:15:34.919 --> 00:15:37.360
[S04] You might be hearing about the nervous system, left, right and centre.

261
00:15:37.389 --> 00:15:39.120
[S04] And you're like, what the heck is that?

262
00:15:39.149 --> 00:15:40.360
[S04] What is the nervous system?

263
00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:44.679
[S04] It's only the command centre of your existence.

264
00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:47.840
[S04] It's like an electrical and chemical system

265
00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:51.000
[S04] that basically runs your entire experience

266
00:15:51.029 --> 00:15:54.240
[S04] in this body and in your mind and in your perception.

267
00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.960
[S04] So essentially, your nervous system is your command centre.

268
00:15:56.990 --> 00:16:01.320
[S04] It consists of your brain, your spinal cord and the nerves in your body.

269
00:16:01.399 --> 00:16:05.360
[S04] Like essentially, you're experiencing the physical world through your senses.

270
00:16:05.379 --> 00:16:07.159
[S04] That's all happening within your nervous system.

271
00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:09.720
[S04] Information is picked up on through your senses

272
00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:12.470
[S04] and then it's perceived and sent and interpreted

273
00:16:12.509 --> 00:16:14.240
[S04] through your nervous system in your brain.

274
00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:17.440
[S04] And then those messages are sent out through the nerves in your body,

275
00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:22.190
[S04] through impulses, all over your body in like a millisecond

276
00:16:22.629 --> 00:16:24.629
[S04] so that you can respond physically.

277
00:16:24.659 --> 00:16:26.960
[S04] So say, for example, you put your hand on a hot stove, right?

278
00:16:27.879 --> 00:16:30.909
[S04] The way that you have the impulse to pull your hand away immediately

279
00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:34.200
[S04] when the heat gets to a certain level is because of your nervous system.

280
00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:38.120
[S04] It perceives the stimuli of touch through the nervous system.

281
00:16:38.149 --> 00:16:40.480
[S04] It interprets it as dangerous in the brain

282
00:16:40.509 --> 00:16:44.519
[S04] and it sends out the electrical impulse to the body, in your neurons,

283
00:16:44.549 --> 00:16:49.039
[S04] to essentially do the movement in your hand to pull that thing away.

284
00:16:49.519 --> 00:16:50.879
[S04] So it controls your breathing.

285
00:16:50.909 --> 00:16:52.320
[S04] It controls your muscle movement.

286
00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:54.720
[S04] It controls how blood flows around your body.

287
00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.120
[S04] It keeps your heart beating.

288
00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.240
[S04] It controls your digestion.

289
00:16:58.559 --> 00:17:00.399
[S04] It controls your perception.

290
00:17:00.759 --> 00:17:05.160
[S04] It controls your whole experience of being a human being, essentially.

291
00:17:05.359 --> 00:17:09.559
[S04] And you can do a much deeper dive on the different parts of the nervous system.

292
00:17:09.589 --> 00:17:12.559
[S04] You've got the central nervous system and the peripheral nervous system.

293
00:17:12.589 --> 00:17:16.680
[S04] And then you have within that the somatic and the autonomic nervous system.

294
00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:20.039
[S04] But for today, we're just going to break it down as simply as possible

295
00:17:20.069 --> 00:17:21.200
[S04] on what you really need to know.

296
00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:23.920
[S04] You have kind of two states.

297
00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:27.119
[S04] When I talk about your nervous system being dysregulated or activated,

298
00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:32.039
[S04] what I'm talking about is a sympathetic nervous system state.

299
00:17:32.319 --> 00:17:35.559
[S04] That is what we know as the fight or flight state.

300
00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:39.640
[S04] That is when your system essentially becomes activated.

301
00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:42.480
[S04] So if you are a healthy human being

302
00:17:42.509 --> 00:17:46.480
[S04] who is not in a state of chronic dysregulation or survival mode,

303
00:17:46.759 --> 00:17:49.880
[S04] it's very normal for you to shift in and out of these two states.

304
00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:54.039
[S04] That's kind of the optimal way of operating.

305
00:17:54.319 --> 00:17:56.680
[S04] I actually see an opposite situation

306
00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:53.079
[S05] It's about being able to be activated if you need to be and being able to shift

307
00:18:53.109 --> 00:18:56.099
[S05] out of activation once the event is over.

308
00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:58.079
[S05] Because like I mentioned, when you're in survival mode,

309
00:18:58.109 --> 00:19:01.019
[S05] you are disconnected from your higher faculties.

310
00:19:01.049 --> 00:19:05.200
[S05] You are in your technically your most animalistic state when you're in survival mode.

311
00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:06.930
[S05] You are reactive.

312
00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:11.299
[S05] You're not able to access your higher faculties, your creative faculties.

313
00:19:11.329 --> 00:19:14.680
[S05] I'm going to just read to you some of the symptoms so that you can now identify

314
00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:18.380
[S05] whether you might be in a state of chronic dysregulation.

315
00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:22.380
[S05] So some of the symptoms physically are fatigue, tension and headaches,

316
00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:26.779
[S05] poor sleep, digestive issues, rapid heartbeat and sensory sensitivity.

317
00:19:26.809 --> 00:19:29.640
[S05] So this is something I know that I'm becoming dysregulated

318
00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:33.880
[S05] when I suddenly just wake up in the morning and I can't like I'm not relaxed.

319
00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:36.700
[S05] Like I need to get out of bed and I feel like I need to move.

320
00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.599
[S05] For me, that's very unusual.

321
00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:42.440
[S05] Some people are like that, but for me, normally I like to get up

322
00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:45.180
[S05] and I like to have a little bit of a slow morning routine.

323
00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:47.880
[S05] And when I feel like I can't do that, when I feel like I'm running

324
00:19:47.910 --> 00:19:52.410
[S05] and I open my eyes early and I'm wide awake, even though I haven't had enough sleep,

325
00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.980
[S05] I know I'm gone into dysregulation.

326
00:19:55.009 --> 00:19:59.700
[S05] Then emotionally, it looks like anxiety or panic, mood swings, numbness.

327
00:19:59.730 --> 00:20:01.089
[S05] That's a really big one.

328
00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:04.559
[S05] Feeling really easily overwhelmed, so like everything is overwhelming,

329
00:20:04.589 --> 00:20:09.900
[S05] even just normal day to day friction of doing certain things.

330
00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:13.180
[S05] And a constant underlying feeling of stress.

331
00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:18.380
[S05] So mental symptoms are racing thoughts, brain fog, overthinking,

332
00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:20.930
[S05] feeling very distracted or unfocused.

333
00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:25.900
[S05] And then behaviorally, this shows up as overworking or staying busy.

334
00:20:25.930 --> 00:20:27.700
[S05] How common is that?

335
00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:31.059
[S05] I feel like I'm calling like 90% of you out right now.

336
00:20:31.089 --> 00:20:34.700
[S05] Avoidance or numbing, if you're not overworking or staying busy,

337
00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:37.960
[S05] then you're avoiding, you're numbing, you're procrastinating,

338
00:20:37.990 --> 00:20:40.700
[S05] you're hiding under a rock.

339
00:20:40.730 --> 00:20:43.720
[S05] Controlling or rigid behavior, so not being able to release control,

340
00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.759
[S05] like trying to control every little thing, either in your relationship

341
00:20:46.789 --> 00:20:49.559
[S05] or in your business, having addictive habits.

342
00:20:49.589 --> 00:20:53.240
[S05] So that's really indicative of being in a dysregulated nervous system state

343
00:20:53.269 --> 00:20:57.880
[S05] because when you are dysregulated, you feel like you have to self soothe.

344
00:20:57.910 --> 00:21:00.140
[S05] And we'll talk about that in a second.

345
00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:04.039
[S05] People pleasing, so the fight or flight state, it's actually longer than that.

346
00:21:04.069 --> 00:21:06.539
[S05] It's fight, flight, freeze or fawn.

347
00:21:06.569 --> 00:21:08.970
[S05] Fawn is people pleasing.

348
00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.990
[S05] Fawn is where we're trying to tune to the energy of the people around us

349
00:21:12.019 --> 00:21:17.140
[S05] and we're trying to get a sense of safety because all of this is to get a sense of safety.

350
00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:21.200
[S05] We're trying to get a sense of safety from getting people's approval

351
00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:25.299
[S05] or getting people's validation because we don't feel safe.

352
00:21:25.329 --> 00:21:29.299
[S05] And another symptom behaviorally is emotional reactivity or shutdown.

353
00:21:29.329 --> 00:21:33.420
[S05] So you're really reactive or sensitive or you're just shutting down, withdrawing.

354
00:21:33.450 --> 00:21:35.839
[S05] Now, we could go into each of the different states

355
00:21:35.869 --> 00:21:38.319
[S05] because there's different things you can do for each of the different states,

356
00:21:38.349 --> 00:21:39.319
[S05] but we don't have time for that today.

357
00:21:39.349 --> 00:21:40.900
[S05] That's not the topic of this video.

358
00:21:40.930 --> 00:21:43.970
[S05] I do go deeper on that in my community if you want to check that out.

359
00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:47.880
[S05] But for now, I just want you to notice if any of that resonated with you

360
00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:51.700
[S05] and how long you may have been in this state if it does resonate with you.

361
00:21:51.730 --> 00:21:55.700
[S05] And then I want you to realize how much potential

362
00:21:55.730 --> 00:21:59.319
[S05] you've been cutting yourself off from by being in this state

363
00:21:59.349 --> 00:22:01.970
[S05] and now by staying in this state.

364
00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:08.140
[S05] You cannot be in creative mode whilst you are in survival mode.

365
00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:13.460
[S05] And one of the scariest things about coming back into a state of regulation

366
00:22:13.490 --> 00:22:16.220
[S05] is you have to come back into your body.

367
00:22:16.250 --> 00:22:19.259
[S05] And when you've been dysregulated for so long,

368
00:22:19.289 --> 00:22:22.400
[S05] you essentially have been disconnected from yourself

369
00:22:22.430 --> 00:22:25.380
[S05] and from your emotions for a really long time.

370
00:22:25.410 --> 00:22:28.240
[S05] So we end up dysregulated and we stay dysregulated

371
00:22:28.269 --> 00:22:31.220
[S05] and then we end up just numbing and self soothing.

372
00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:33.680
[S05] This is why people have addictive patterns.

373
00:22:33.710 --> 00:22:35.680
[S05] This is why people scroll so much.

374
00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:37.039
[S05] This is why we binge eat.

375
00:22:37.069 --> 00:22:39.500
[S05] This is why we have shopping addictions.

376
00:22:39.529 --> 00:22:45.539
[S05] Because we're doing everything we can to numb and distract ourselves

377
00:22:45.569 --> 00:22:50.720
[S05] rather than coming back into our body, bringing our awareness back into the here and now

378
00:22:50.750 --> 00:22:54.960
[S05] because it feels too painful for our awareness to be in the here and now

379
00:22:54.990 --> 00:22:58.259
[S05] because that would require us reconnecting with ourselves

380
00:22:58.289 --> 00:23:03.019
[S05] and feeling emotions that we've probably been avoiding feeling.

381
00:23:03.049 --> 00:23:05.119
[S05] And so this is the biggest key I'm going to give you

382
00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:06.900
[S05] and it's something you can't bypass.

383
00:23:06.930 --> 00:23:10.809
[S05] The path back to regulation is feeling.

384
00:23:10.839 --> 00:23:12.420
[S05] The good, the bad, the ugly.

385
00:23:12.440 --> 00:23:16.299
[S05] You have to let yourself feel what you've been avoiding.

386
00:23:16.329 --> 00:23:18.880
[S05] And this is going to help you break so many habits

387
00:23:18.900 --> 00:23:21.160
[S05] when you actually start to do this and go to the root cause

388
00:23:21.190 --> 00:23:24.160
[S05] and you're going to have to kind of microdose this and build it up.

389
00:23:24.190 --> 00:23:26.799
[S05] It's not going to be something you can like one and done

390
00:23:26.829 --> 00:23:29.799
[S05] and just become magically amazingly regulated all of a sudden.

391
00:23:29.829 --> 00:23:34.130
[S05] No, it happens through consistency over time.

392
00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:38.220
[S05] Consistently choosing something that's regulating over something that's self soothing.

393
00:24:14.670 --> 00:24:20.069
[S06] I was, I had given up so many of my habits. It was a long time, really, really long times

394
00:24:20.099 --> 00:24:23.410
[S06] as I smoked a cigarette. I smoked a cigarette, probably the last time I smoked a cigarette

395
00:24:23.440 --> 00:24:28.130
[S06] was, I don't know, six years ago or seven years ago. And I kind of just did it because

396
00:24:28.160 --> 00:24:32.910
[S06] people at work were doing it. I wasn't really ever addicted, but I lost the desire for

397
00:24:32.940 --> 00:24:38.470
[S06] it completely, especially as I became more regulated. And I remember one day, I was

398
00:24:38.500 --> 00:24:42.880
[S06] on the way to the airport and something happened and I was feeling a lot of anxiety.

399
00:24:42.910 --> 00:24:46.529
[S06] And I hadn't felt that much anxiety in a really long time. And there was a woman

400
00:24:46.559 --> 00:24:51.259
[S06] outside the airport smoking a cigarette. And I got the feeling of desire in my body

401
00:24:51.289 --> 00:24:55.000
[S06] that I wanted a cigarette in that moment. Out of the blue, it came out of nowhere.

402
00:24:55.029 --> 00:25:01.950
[S06] And I immediately made that link. That desire to numb and self-soothe and smoke a cigarette

403
00:25:01.980 --> 00:25:07.440
[S06] is there because I feel very anxious right now. So the cigarette only would feel good

404
00:25:07.470 --> 00:25:11.230
[S06] because it would soothe the anxiety. And so if I want to get rid of the desire for

405
00:25:11.259 --> 00:25:14.690
[S06] the cigarette, I need to look at why is the anxiety there that needs soothing in the

406
00:25:14.720 --> 00:25:17.759
[S06] first place? Because if I get rid of the anxiety, the desire for the cigarette is

407
00:25:17.789 --> 00:25:21.400
[S06] going to go away. Now, I didn't, the desire wasn't that strong that I actually wanted

408
00:25:21.420 --> 00:25:25.009
[S06] to go and do it. And if you smoke, no judgment. But this just gave me so much perspective

409
00:25:25.029 --> 00:25:29.230
[S06] as to why we have the habits that we have and why they're so hard to kick. It's because

410
00:25:29.259 --> 00:25:36.529
[S06] they're serving us. They are soothing us. They are tending to an emotion or to something

411
00:25:36.559 --> 00:25:41.859
[S06] internally that we don't want to tend to. It's like putting a Band-Aid over it. And

412
00:25:41.890 --> 00:25:47.250
[S06] for a while, maybe that Band-Aid is helping you. Maybe it's working for you. But the

413
00:25:47.279 --> 00:25:52.190
[S06] self-soothing behaviours, they kind of just give you a temporary relief in the moment.

414
00:25:52.220 --> 00:25:55.640
[S06] They don't regulate your nervous system. Okay, so this is where I'm going to distinguish

415
00:25:55.670 --> 00:25:59.140
[S06] and I'm going to give you some actual practices that do regulate your nervous system. You've

416
00:25:59.170 --> 00:26:02.829
[S06] got self-soothing behaviours that numb and distract you and disconnect you, that give

417
00:26:02.859 --> 00:26:07.359
[S06] you temporary relief in the moment, which sometimes we need that. Okay, that's fine.

418
00:26:07.390 --> 00:26:12.119
[S06] But they don't actually signal safety to your body. They don't actually regulate your

419
00:26:12.150 --> 00:26:18.410
[S06] nervous system. They don't actually bring you to a state of calm. What does do that

420
00:26:18.440 --> 00:26:23.559
[S06] and what does bring you out of survival more gradually with consistency is regulating

421
00:26:23.589 --> 00:26:28.049
[S06] behaviours and regulating practices. Okay. So these are really different to self-soothing

422
00:26:28.079 --> 00:26:31.660
[S06] behaviours. Self-soothing behaviours are things that disconnect you from your body

